{"term":"frank","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f7f41fdd49a5043263","definition":"Honest, especially in a manner that seems slightly blunt; candid; not reserved or disguised.","example":"May I be frank with you?","pos":"adj","synonyms":["unreserved","undisguised","free-spoken"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b1f11b57fe559fa24f","definition":"Unmistakable, clinically obvious, self-evident.","example":"The research probes whether treating pre-diabetes with metformin can prevent progression to frank diabetes.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4f28a2ad9cb9926358","definition":"Unbounded by restrictions, limitations, etc.; free.","example":"It is of frank gift.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9aa4123fec62b13808","definition":"Liberal; generous; profuse.","example":"Frank of Civilities that cost them nothing.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1ade4f4d38659bd5c5","definition":"Unrestrained; loose; licentious.","example":"Over the fields, in his franke lustinesse,\nAnd all the champain o're he soared light.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, obsolete","register":"derogatory, obsolete","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d8597f1844c0c37825","definition":"Free postage, a right exercised by governments (usually with definite article).","example":"October 5, 1780, William Cowper, letter to Rev. William Unwin\nI have said so much, that, if I had not a frank, I must burn my letter and begin again.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c57db80f2aea867bc1","definition":"The notice on an envelope where a stamp would normally be found.","example":"But, although her friends were kind, Lady Anne was not easy; neither daughter made her appearance, nor did she receive a letter to account for their silence. She remembered, indeed, that Charles Penrhyn could not get franks now, and her daughters knew she would not pay postage; and she had commanded Helen to work night and day, saying, \"surely they can give her common materials.\"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a16e597ea03cfe94e4","definition":"To place a frank on an envelope.","example":"It will be so ridiculous to see all his letters directed to him with an M.P.—But do you know, he says, he will never frank for me?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d17000f6ea384ad92e","definition":"To exempt from charge for postage, as a letter, package, or packet, etc.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:50b3edf383fe56dbd3","definition":"To send by public conveyance free of expense.","example":"1850-1859, Charles Dickens, Household Words\nThis required extensive correspondence; so, in the next place, the privilege of franking letters in reference to the emigrants' registration office, was obtained—much to the indignation of red tapists.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:55b441c1f8574b8d94","definition":"A hot dog or sausage.","example":"Buy a package of franks for the barbecue.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["frankfurt","frankfurter"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7583ffc7ac49f90004","definition":"The grey heron.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK","register":"UK","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9f02d98d57b87bb995","definition":"A pigsty.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ba4a3c9ceb1637596b","definition":"To shut up in a frank or sty; to pen up; hence, to cram; to fatten.","example":"Marry, as for Clarence, he is well repaid;\nHe is franked up to fatting for his pains","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7a2586a888a249b555","definition":"Obsolete form of franc, former French coins, moneys of account, and currency.","example":"Frank, or Franc, an ancient coin, either of gold or ſilver, ſtruck and current in France. The value of the gold frank was ſomewhat more than that of the gold crown; the ſilver frank was a third of the gold one; this coin is long out of uſe, though the term is ſtill retained as the name of a money of account; in which ſenſe it is equivalent to the livre, or twenty ſols.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of, historical, obsolete","register":"alt-of, historical, obsolete","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:11fda44bdb87033465","definition":"One of the Franks, a Germanic federation that inhabited parts of what are now France, the Low Countries and Germany.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e6f0ed41f2cc3f290e","definition":"Frenchman.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6c3941ae336f15c8ad","definition":"A male given name from the Germanic languages.","example":"Mrs. Ford. How now, sweet Frank! why art thou melancholy?","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frank bank","frank-fee","frankly","frank-marriage","frankness","frankpledge","franksome","to be frank","unfrank","overfrank","frankable","prefranked","unfranked","Frank-Tamm formula","Frank-ter Haar syndrome"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Frank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1c88fada18bc3a14e4","definition":"A diminutive of the male given name Francis.","example":"Your name is Francis, is it?\nFrank, sir.\nYour name is Francis. There was never a St. Frank. That's a name for gangsters and politicians.","pos":"name","synon